WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.569
Ellaria Sand: Before the Seven Kingdoms, before
the Iron Throne, there was Dorne. Twelve thousand

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:13.570
years ago, the First Men crossed the land
bridge from Essos to here. Of course, they

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.589
were men, so they soon broke it.

00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:21.520
Then, while their cousins to the North built
kingdoms, the Dornish squabbled over land,

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:30.859
water, and wives for centuries. Until Nymeria,
a warrior princess in Essos.

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:36.140
She led a fleet of ten thousand ships across
the Narrow Sea to Dorne. Almost all of the

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:44.610
petty lords made it clear that she wasn't
welcome. All but one. Mors of House Martell.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:51.400
He saw in her a strength to match any man,
including his rivals. After she accepted his

00:00:51.400 --> 00:01:03.800
marriage offer, she set fire 

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:41.470
to her ships. For 

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:48.860
fifty leagues, the coast was bright as day,
and in the burning light, Princess Nymeria

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:56.250
named Mors Martell the Prince of Dorne, in
the style of her people. Dorne would be her

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:00.360
home or her grave.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:08.520
For many years, Nymeria and Mors waged war
against all rivals. The Jordaynes, Blackmonts,

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:16.180
Qorgyles, and even the mighty House Yronwood.
They sent no fewer than six self-styled "kings"

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:22.970
to the Wall in golden chains. After Mors fell
in battle, Nymeria took command of his armies

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.150
and united Dorne in two years.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:30.730
She ruled for twenty-seven more, and though
she married again, those husbands were little

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:39.319
more than councilors and consorts. Dorne was
Nymeria, and Nymeria was Dorne.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:44.050
She survived a dozen attempts on her life,
put down two rebellions, and threw back two

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:50.450
invasions. And when at last, she died, her
eldest child succeeded her (her daughter,

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:56.900
not her son), and Dorne followed her because
Nymeria had proven that women were equal to

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.269
men, if not better.

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:07.260
"Unbowed, unbent, unbroken." The words of
House Martell. The words of Dorne. Men may

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:14.680
forget, but women always remember. When we
were divided, Nymeria united us. When we were

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:17.460
invaded, Meria defended us.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:23.080
Varys: Westeros has mighty rivers, but none
of them compare to the Rhoyne. It is said

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:29.170
that there is no stream or puddle in western
Essos but drains to Mother Rhoyne. No doubt,

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:32.440
an exaggeration. Until one sees the river.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:38.200
At its widest, a man in the center can't see
a shore to either side. The greatest of Mother

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:43.459
Rhoyne's children were the Rhoynar, a civilization
as ancient and grand as Old Ghis.

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:48.849
Fishers, traders, scholars, workers of wood,
stone, and metal, the Rhoynar raised their

00:03:48.849 --> 00:03:53.780
elegant cities from the headwaters of the
Rhoyne down to her mouth, each lovelier than

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:54.879
the last.

00:03:54.879 --> 00:04:00.300
For many centuries, the Rhoynar lived in relative
peace. When invaders swept down from the hills,

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:07.079
the Rhoynar women and men would don silver-scaled
armor, fish head helms, tall spears, and turtle

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.810
shell shields.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:13.430
If the enemy did not laugh themselves away,
it was said that Mother Rhoyne would whisper

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:18.680
the enemy's secrets to her children, and the
Rhoynish wizards could raise watery walls

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.829
to drown their foes.

00:04:20.829 --> 00:04:26.310
Whatever magic the Rhoynar may have had, it
wasn't enough. When Valyrian colonists first

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:31.259
arrived, the Rhoynar embraced them, for all
men were welcome to share the bounty of Mother

00:04:31.259 --> 00:04:32.259
Rhoyne.

00:04:32.259 --> 00:04:37.830
Perhaps a water people should have been more
cautious of strangers who exulted fire and

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:43.479
blood. Legend has it that one day the Valyrians
netted and butchered one of the giant turtles

00:04:43.479 --> 00:04:45.310
the Rhoynar held sacred.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:51.830
As a result, thousands were killed or enslaved,
cities and towns were burned, drowned, and

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:56.650
rebuilt. In these wars, the Valyrians emerged
as victorious more often than not.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:01.680
The princes of the Rhoynish cities, fiercely
proud of their independence, fought alone,

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:05.060
whilst the Valyrian colonies aided one another.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:10.340
Eventually, the Rhoynish princes ceased their
squabbling and united behind Prince Garin,

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:17.400
who led the largest army Essos had ever seen
against 100,000 Valyrian colonists, 100 war

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.919
elephants, and three dragonlords.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:25.319
Thousands burned, but thousands more sheltered
in the shallows of the river whilst the Rhoynish

00:05:25.319 --> 00:05:30.210
wizards raised enormous water spouts against
the foes' dragons.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:36.830
Rhoynish archers brought down two of the dragons
whilst the third fled wounded, and thereafter

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.509
the Rhoynar named Garin "the Great."

00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:45.180
But Mother Valyria proved just as caring as
Mother Rhoyne. When Garin the Great marched

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:50.900
his army against Volantis, three hundred Valyrian
dragons descended from the sky.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:54.370
Tens of thousands burned whilst others rushed
into the river.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:59.500
But the fire burned so hot that the waters
boiled and turned to steam. Garin the Great

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:04.840
was captured alive and made to watch as Valyrians
butchered every last man, so many that their

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:09.599
blood turned the great harbor of Volantis
red as far as the eye could see.

00:06:09.599 --> 00:06:14.310
Then they forced Garin to watch as they marched
on his own city and enslaved all the women

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.110
and children his army had left behind.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:22.230
The singers claimed that Prince Garin called
out Mother Rhoyne to curse the Valyrians,

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:26.830
and she, in turn, flooded the city with foul
waters and a damp fog that caused the skin

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:31.870
of the Valyrians to harden and crack, and
thus was born greyscale.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:38.400
Qyburn: Few afflictions are more feared than
greyscale, and far past the point of reason.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:43.830
A legend calls it "Prince Garin's curse,"
after an ancient eastern prince whom the Valyrians

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:48.490
hung in a cage and forced to watch the immolation
of his city and people.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:53.289
As his city burned under dragonflame, this
prince called on his god for vengeance, and

00:06:53.289 --> 00:06:58.750
a thick fog of foul humors rose from the Rhoyne
to smother the Valyrians with greyscale.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:04.030
But if diseases could be called down by the
vengeful, we would have no health in the world.

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:09.090
More likely the disease predates the Valyrians
entirely, confined to some remote region of

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:14.020
Essos, and only spread throughout the world
once the Valyrians linked the continent with

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:15.940
roads and dragons.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:22.849
Fearing a similar fate, another Rhoynish ruler,
Princess Nymeria, led her own people into

00:07:22.849 --> 00:07:30.331
every ship, skiff, and raft they had and fled
Essos. Eventually, after much hardship, they

00:07:30.331 --> 00:07:33.680
landed in sunswept and bone dry Dorne.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:41.270
Oberyn Martell: "Unbowed, Unbent, Unbroken."
The words of House Martell. A promise to our

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:45.550
enemies and a challenge to our lovers.

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:49.909
Thousands of years ago, the warrior queen
Nymeria crossed into Dorne from Essos, fleeing

00:07:49.909 --> 00:07:56.530
the dragonlords of Valyria. After she landed,
she burned her ships, all ten thousand of

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.590
them, so no cowards could slink home.

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:06.289
What a woman. Dornish in spirit before she
ever was in flesh.

00:08:06.289 --> 00:08:11.051
She was lucky to land in Dorne, where powerful
women are not locked away in septs and the

00:08:11.051 --> 00:08:18.100
beds of old men. My ancestor, Mors Martell,
saw her and desired her, and proved that where

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.539
armies fail, a tongue may succeed.

00:08:21.539 --> 00:08:29.620
Wedding his strength to hers, his spear to
her sun, they subdued all of his rivals together.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:35.500
After the tradition of her people, House Martell
then ruled Dorne as Princes, not kings, unless

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:37.570
the eldest child was a daughter.

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:44.250
For unlike the rest of Westeros, our loyalty
is not commanded by a c***. We follow a Prince

00:08:44.250 --> 00:09:05.100
or a Princess Martell just 

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:15.460
the same.

